<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.25	    + 88	    19.00     19.55</p>
<p>91-Day	19.75	    + 80	    19.69     19.80</p>
<p>182-Day     20.98	    + 58	    20.77     20.99</p>
<p>350-Day     20.94				20.78     21.00</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 20.24 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   3.22 bln pesos     4.03</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   5.51 bln pesos     6.89</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.75 bln pesos     4.69</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.23 bln pesos     3.72</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.90 on demand of 14.71 billion pesos compared with 2.76 the week before, on demand of 8.29 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  30    basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   5    basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  1    basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			  6    basis points</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
